--
iostream with cerr, operator<<, and std::endl in C++11.
Invariant violation: std::less<std::_V2::error_category>::~less
destructor symbol not found. Triggered by <system_error> header
on some g++ 13 header versions (Ubuntu 24.04 CI).
The standard stream objects are now defined and constructed
([iostream.objects.overview]/3), so the program verifies without bounds;
it was a conversion check with loop and recursion bounds because
std::cerr was nondeterministic.
